<!--
    GH-7190: V850 BranchLessThen (SXB; CMP; BLT) decompiles to overflow-flag garbage.

    Source loop:   do { ... } while (cVar5 < 8);   (signed byte counter compare)
    The V850 SLEIGH set_OV_neg macro models the OV flag via a sub-register sign
    shift instead of `A s< 0`, so the BLT condition lifts to the p-code idiom
      INT_SLESS(V+K,0) != ( byte_sign(V) && INT_SLESS(-1, V+K) ).
    The default S3 simplification pool cannot see through the constant offset
    (V + K) plus the sub-register sign test, so the convoluted boolean leaks into
    the rendered C instead of collapsing to a clean signed less-than.

    Stage / sub-stage: S3 simplification-quiescence (new named rule RuleOvLessSimplify).
    P0 assertion: option ovlesssimplify off|on (default off = upstream byte-identical).
    Pass 1 (default off): assertion #1 proves the bug reproduces today.
    Pass 2 (option ovlesssimplify on): assertion #2 proves the rule collapses the
    condition to a clean `cVar5 < '\b'` (signed byte compare against 8).
-->
